==============================================================================
VCACHE-3D  --  power model
==============================================================================
  base tier 3.0 GHz / 0.95 V   cache tier 1.5 GHz / 0.75 V

operating point                      base   dielet   scrub    total
                                       mW       mW      mW       mW
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
idle (retention, no traffic)         1866      540    0.04     2406
light (0.05 req/cyc)                 1873     1130    0.04     3003
nominal (0.30 req/cyc)               1908     1721    0.04     3630
peak (1.00 req/cyc, 3 slices)        2007     1873    0.00     3880

  peak total          3.88 W
  nominal total       3.63 W
  dielet peak (each)  0.62 W   over 10.57 mm^2
  dielet power density 0.059 W/mm^2  (thermal model uses this as the stacked-layer source term)

  Energy per L3 hit:
    base-die way (0..3) :   15.1 pJ  (0.24 pJ/byte)
    stacked way (4..15):   59.7 pJ  (0.93 pJ/byte)

  Note: the stacked hit costs more energy per access than the base-die
  hit because of the bond link, but far less than the DRAM access it
  replaces (~20 pJ/byte for DDR5), which is the entire point of the dielet.

  Power management implemented in RTL (rtl/power/):
    * per-bank sleep / deep-sleep / retention (bank_sleep[31:0])
    * 8 DVFS levels with a voltage/frequency handshake
    * thermal throttle driven by 16 on-dielet sensors
    * scrub suppression while throttled
